From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Skia: add ppc64le Power ISA 2.07 VSX CPU raster optimizations

Enable ppc64le LE VSX SIMD acceleration (ISA 2.07 / POWER8 floor, compatible
with both -mcpu=power8 and -mcpu=power9) in WebKit's bundled Skia CPU raster
paths under Source/ThirdParty/skia/:

1. include/private/SkFeatures.h + src/opts/SkOpts_SetTarget.h:
   Define SK_PPC_HAS_VSX on little-endian 64-bit Power when __VSX__ and
   __POWER8_VECTOR__ are active, routing SK_OPTS_NS=vsx.
2. src/core/SkVx.h:
   Add VSX specializations for if_then_else, any, all, ceil, floor, trunc,
   sqrt, abs, lrint, saturated_add (vec_adds), and strided_load4 (vec_perm),
   eliminating scalar libm calls and lane-by-lane spill loops.
3. src/opts/SkRasterPipeline_opts.h (SKRP_CPU_VSX):
   Replace scalar SKRP_CPU_SCALAR fallback (stride 1, lowp disabled) with
   4-wide highp (N=4) and 8-wide lowp (N=8, SKRP_NARROW_STAGES=0) VSX SIMD
   primitives, vectorized load2/store2/load4/store4 transposes, and
   vectorized lowp::cast / mad / nmad / round_F_to_U16 / div255 / max_intr /
   min_intr.
4. src/opts/SkSwizzler_opts.inc:
   Add VSX paths for all 12 swizzler functions (RGBA_to_BGRA, RGBA_to_rgbA,
   RGBA_to_bgrA, inverted_CMYK_to_RGB1, inverted_CMYK_to_BGR1, rgbA_to_RGBA,
   rgbA_to_BGRA, gray_to_RGB1, grayA_to_RGBA, grayA_to_rgbA, RGB_to_RGB1,
   RGB_to_BGR1).
5. src/opts/SkBlitRow_opts.h:
   Add 4-pixel-per-iteration VSX blit_row_s32a_opaque using vec_mladd/vec_adds.
6. src/opts/SkBlitMask_opts.h:
   Add 8-pixel-per-iteration VSX blit_mask_d32_a8_{black,opaque,general}
   bypassing GCC's non-inlined generic Sk4px/MapDstAlpha fallback.
7. src/opts/SkBitmapProcState_opts.h:
   Add 2-pixel batched Y-first VSX S32_alpha_D32_filter_DX bilinear filter
   with scalar tail.

Verified on native POWER9 against scalar portable oracle (--verify ref_p8)
and audited with objdump -M power8 vs -M power9 (0 ISA 3.0 leaks, 0 vabsdu).
